<p>France and the United Kingdom convened an international summit in Paris on April 17 to advance plans for restoring freedom of navigation in the Strait of Hormuz, the narrow shipping route heavily affected by the war involving the United States, Israel and Iran. President Emmanuel Macron and Prime Minister Keir Starmer gathered roughly 30 to 40 countries to discuss a future multinational maritime mission that would help secure shipping and trade once conditions permit, with several reports noting the United States was not part of the planning for this initiative. The European effort reflects a practical push to protect global energy flows and lower market strain after the blockade of the strait sent energy prices higher. The meeting also highlighted a diplomatic opening: European allies are signaling they are prepared to help stabilize a vital trade chokepoint after the conflict, even as they differ over how closely any eventual mission should be tied to the United States or NATO.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/HAlMtjF_rUBMeLQ3lPZ6YEg2kcTJO7k6Uu3kQUG5vzhsLTq2JgmxtiqpGrQ-W33-yBybi_04-kjlrvMXqXaQSimONyfe-j7LaFfl6c-1pGkyTeZN8HvtvIV35XmMCiFXEIBCVJz21Gt5xBPV4qvjyWSAsnfTSGxrepCAoxi-Fg' alt='French President Emmanuel Macron and UK Prime Minister Keir Starmer at the Paris summit on reopening the Strait of Hormuz.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Signal to Washington: The Straits Times reported the Paris meeting was also meant to show the United States that close allies are prepared to help restore freedom of navigation in Hormuz once conditions allow.</li><li>Coalition design dispute: A key unresolved issue is whether any eventual mission would remain under European political control or be linked to US and NATO structures, with Berlin favoring the latter approach.</li><li>Wider attendance: SCMP reported that China was among the Asian countries engaging with the Paris summit, indicating the organizers were seeking support beyond Europe and the Gulf states.</li><li>Follow-up with Washington: The Financial Times reported Macron and Starmer were expected to brief President Trump after the meeting, suggesting Europe still wanted coordination with the US after first convening allies on its own.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>France and the United Kingdom: Paris and London are jointly organizing a maritime security plan meant to show allies can help restore shipping through Hormuz while Europe positions itself as not being a party to the war. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/china/diplomacy/article/3350404/why-europe-testing-third-way-hormuz-without-us-israel-and-iran'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Germany: Politico reports Chancellor Friedrich Merz favors a &#x27;coalition of the willing&#x27; with US involvement and is discussing a NATO-linked approach, putting Berlin on a different track from Macron. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/podcast/berlin-playbook-podcast/merz-gegen-macron-streit-um-die-strase-von-hormus/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>European analysts and diplomats: SCMP frames the initiative as a European &#x27;third way&#x27; — an effort to shape the postwar maritime outcome through independent diplomacy rather than simply fold into Washington&#x27;s lead. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/china/diplomacy/article/3350404/why-europe-testing-third-way-hormuz-without-us-israel-and-iran'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/macron-starmer-hold-international-summit-on-reopening-strait-of-hormuz/article70872634.ece'>Macron, Starmer hold international summit on reopening Strait of Hormuz</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/macron-starmer-rally-allies-to-mull-over-hormuz-mission'>Macron, Starmer rally allies to mull over Hormuz mission</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/china/diplomacy/article/3350404/why-europe-testing-third-way-hormuz-without-us-israel-and-iran'>Europe tests ‘third way’ on Hormuz without the US, Israel and Iran. Will it work?</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/macron-starmer-hold-international-summit-reopening-strait-hormuz-132126875'>Macron and Starmer hold international summit on reopening the Strait of Hormuz</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/a348e5e0-c9d3-424c-b8a9-7903fa817b7d'>Macron and Starmer to hold summit on plan to secure Strait of Hormuz</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/macron-starmer-rally-allies-mull-hormuz-mission'>Macron, Starmer rally allies to mull Hormuz mission</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/podcast/berlin-playbook-podcast/merz-gegen-macron-streit-um-die-strase-von-hormus/'>Merz gegen Macron – Streit um die Straße von Hormus</a> - politico.eu</li></ul>